AMDGPU: 1 MiB command-buffer blocks.

A program with more than one block is replayed block by block from the host. The engine's pp2048 chunk graph
(~980 dispatches) spilled into a second 128 KiB block, and the GPU sat idle 0.50-0.69 ms at the block boundary
(dispatch ~886 of the chunk) in every timeline run. With one 1 MiB block the chunk graph is a single submission:
the idle is gone, the other inter-dispatch gaps are unchanged (6.74 vs 6.77 ms per chunk).

diff --git a/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/amdgpu/aql_program_builder.h b/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/amdgpu/aql_program_builder.h
index 74a62c132..99761568b 100644
--- a/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/amdgpu/aql_program_builder.h
+++ b/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/amdgpu/aql_program_builder.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ extern "C" {
 
 enum {
   // Default usable bytes per command-buffer block.
-  IREE_HAL_AMDGPU_AQL_PROGRAM_DEFAULT_BLOCK_SIZE = 128 * 1024,
+  IREE_HAL_AMDGPU_AQL_PROGRAM_DEFAULT_BLOCK_SIZE = 1024 * 1024,
   // Minimum usable bytes per command-buffer block.
   IREE_HAL_AMDGPU_AQL_PROGRAM_MIN_BLOCK_SIZE = 256,
 };
